"- Winter daylight is short (gone before 5 p.m. in December), so a headlamp becomes core gear.\n- 200–400 lumens is enough for trails; check the burn time at each setting, not just peak output.\n- Lithium-ion loses 20–30% capacity near freezing: keep the lamp in an inside pocket and pick one with AAA lithium backup (alkaline is worst in cold).\n- Get a red-light mode and at least IPX4 sealing (IPX7 for stream crossings).\n- Under 100 g, fits over a beanie, buttons usable with gloves.\n- Pick for most hikers: 300–400 lumen rechargeable with AAA backup, red light, IPX4+, about $30–45."
